    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The U.S. Navy is undertaking a significant infrastructure improvement project at its shipyards, focusing on the 4 shipyards. A decommissioned frigate, USS Klakring (FFG-42), was sunk as part of a sinking exercise with Royal Navy forces. The U.S. plans to transfer three King Air turboprop planes equipped for maritime domain awareness operations to the Philippine Coast Guard. The 94th Army Air and Missile Defense Command hosted a Pacific Air Combat Simulation (PACSIM) exercise, featuring U.S., Japanese, and Australian militaries. The U.S. Army has selected five companies to deliver prototypes of a missile capable of hitting moving, long-range maritime targets to the U.S. Army. The U.S. Coast Guard is currently in transit, and the 104th Fighter Wing held a Change of Responsibility and Retirement Ceremony honoring Command Sgt. Maj. Ronald Smith. The 94th Army Air and Missile Defense Command hosted a Pacific Air Combat Simulation (PACSIM) exercise.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
